  "reasoning": "The defendant operated a jewelry processing workshop that generated waste water containing heavy metals (chromium and nickel). The waste water was not treated and was directly discharged into a sewage system, resulting in concentrations far exceeding legal standards (4.4 times for chromium, 9.6 times for nickel). This conduct constitutes illegal discharge of pollutants into water bodies, which is punishable under the environmental pollution provisions of the Criminal Law (Article 338). No other criminal conduct is described, so the appropriate charge is the crime of illegal discharge of pollutants.",
